<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mexico</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mexico is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> whose central valley was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>. After the Spanish conquest of 1519 to 1521, it became the core of the viceroyalty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, one of the richest parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> thanks to its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines. Mexico gained independence in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexico.jpg" alt="Mexico" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omar Alejandro Covarrubias Neri, 9 April 2006.; Based on the 1968 arms by Francisco Eppens Helguera and Juan Manuel Gabino Villascán. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mexico.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
